 nutritional sciences (GAINS): A systematic review and reporting framework for future research#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42],"#GenAI in nutritional sciences (GAINS): A systematic review and reporting framework for future research#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[42,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/ER58GSBL","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/VRLTSRBA?page=1&annotation=6DLJ7QRW","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/VRLTSRBA?page=1&annotation=NNLTWEBC","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/VRLTSRBA?page=1&annotation=ZKFH63WL","line":42}],"metadata":{"Title":"GenAI in nutritional sciences (GAINS): A systematic review and reporting framework for future research","Authors":"Bettina Hieronimus, Maria-Laura Lopez-Aguirre, Marc Birringer, Maren Podszun","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.1016/j.nutres.2025.09.011","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This pre-registered systematic review (CRD42025619448) aimed to synthesize current evidence on the quality of nutritional advice provided by LLM-powered chatbot","Findings":"While the chatbots in the included studies demonstrate potential as tools for nutrition advice, caution is necessary as they tend to be less effective with complex cases and may occasionally produce incorrect responses","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"Key limitations included the frequent use of subjective or poorly defined assessment measures as well as a lack of reproducibility testing.","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1k4mq4s","at":1774939660322}},"smart_blocks:hieronimusGenAINutritionalSciences2025a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.02375249,0.03295926,0.02801267,-0.01963528,0.00616079,0.00921427,-0.01580156,0.0537